\chapter{Assembly}

This is the only file that will carry \texttt{@@o} directives. The concept
chapters never name an output path. They define chunks, and this file routes
those chunks to the files the build expects, so the layout can change without
touching a single narrative.

Stage one routes the scaffold, the rope model, the topology, the renderer, and
the page. Each route below names one file and the chunk that fills it.

